  "body": "Part of #655. Filed on the maintainer's word (question dialog, 2026-11-12). It carries out his answer on #655 (2026-11-10): \"layer Agents.md and refer to its UI agent from the main one. The sub agents.md should live with the UI crates as a steering document that gets ingested by the coding agent as an addendum\".\n\nDone means: `crates/ui/AGENTS.md` holds the UI laws that are now spread over the root file and memory of past reviews - layering (ui -> app -> flecs, no world-level calls from panels), everything is a command, where a control for one setup lives (the setup's own page; see #1104), plain-English text (no G-code jargon), the form seam, 400-line files, structural tests instead of pixel snapshots, icons and their sources (our own SVG masters and Tabler; nothing from SolidCraft without recorded permission, see #661); the root AGENTS.md links it; the path is added to the process-file sync list (the `git checkout upstream/main -- ...` command and the list in \"Process files sync\"); `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION` bumped and announced on #681. Text only: no rule is changed, only gathered.",
